  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P obligated $1.1B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The company won 30 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $35.2M, and obligations are down 51.3% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $103M in FY21 to a peak of $2.3B in FY24, then moved to $2.2B in FY25 and to $1.1B in FY26. Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing is the dominant market for the company at $995M this year. Engineering Services accounted for $39.5M, Motor Vehicle Gasoline Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing accounted for $19.8M, and Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing accounted for $102K in FY2026 to date. Several listed NAICS categories show $0 in obligations this year, including Current-Carrying Wiring Device Manufacturing, Other Electronic Component Manufacturing, and Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services. Current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in some tables reflect total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P's federal business trended year to year?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $103M in FY21 to $604M in FY22, then to $2.1B in FY23 and $2.3B in FY24 before edging to $2.2B in FY25 and $1.1B in FY26. The company is seeing a year-over-year decline, with obligations down 51.3% in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Bae Systems Land and Armaments L P's dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing accounted for $995M of obligations in FY2026 to date, making it the clear concentration. Engineering Services ($39.5M) and Motor Vehicle Gasoline Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing ($19.8M) are secondary markets, while Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing is $102K this year and several NAICS categories show $0."
      }
